      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T18:33:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously, there was a check on `num_vdos`, and an invalid value would not write anything to `vdo`. Now, an invalid value of `vdo_index` will write to `vdo` up to that index. Furthermore, it now appears possible to use this function to read more times from `vdos` than it actually contains elements. Both of these properties seem surprising to me.\n\nIs this what the RTS54xx actually does?",
      "revId": "b9914d391a6d94f86ba6e2502f42b79f068f7f72",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5d8f1b5e_7fa2f8f6",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/emul_realtek_rts54xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 801,
      "author": {
        "id": 3773521
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-27T14:35:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this check was redundant, because `get_vdo.vdo_req.num_vdos` is defined as only 3 bits so max value is 7. I can add check for this but compiler already enforce check for `num_vdos`.\n\nI don\u0027t think we write up to `vdo_index`. We write the VDO at specific index meaning we can have VDOs arr as [0,0,0,0x1111,0,0] but this is what we want. \n\nI also check `vdo_index \u003c RTS54XX_VDO_MAX_NUM` so it is not possible to read outside of arr. \n\nRtk spec says that we pass list of VDO types to `get_vdo` to specify what types we want to get. For `set_vdo` we have list `[uint8_t type1, uint32_t vdo1, uint8_t type2, uint32_t vdo2 ... ]`.   \n\nLet me know if I missed something. \n\n```\nstruct get_vdo_req {\n\t...\n\tunion get_vdo_t vdo_req;\n\tuint8_t vdo_type[7];\n} get_vdo;\n\nunion get_vdo_t {\n\tstruct {\n\t\tuint8_t num_vdos : 3;\n\t\tuint8_t vdo_origin : 2;\n\t\tuint8_t reserved : 3;\n\t};\n\tuint8_t raw_value;\n};\n```",
      "parentUuid": "55b9b0aa_8ef2335f",
      "revId": "b9914d391a6d94f86ba6e2502f42b79f068f7f72",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a05c257a_03cada7c",
        "filename": "zephyr/emul/emul_realtek_rts54xx.c",
